//! The `position-try-order` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property allows
//! you to prioritize the `position-try-fallbacks` option applied to an anchor-positioned element
//! when it first renders, based on which option creates the most space around the element in the
//! given direction.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: normal | <try-size>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#propdef-position-try-order
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/position-try-order
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
